    "DOI": "10.1177/1940082920915651",
    "title": "Sustainability of Timor Deer in Captivity: Captive Breeding Systems in West Java, Indonesia",
    "notes": "The cycleDuration is longer than the AgeAtSalughter because the cycle starts from the fetus of the animal to be slaughtered ( includes 250\u2009days of pregnancy). 'The urea, plastic and brick inputs to the farmed system were not included in the deer rearing cycle as they were assumed to be used for the construction of the forage garden, which would be a separate site & cycle.",
